C03: PDF composer instruction in plain prose, shorter opening (PDF1693)

In PDF1691 the English drafts for «Summarize informe.pdf.» came out as lowercase «key: value» lines («document: informe.pdf, pages: 2 / headings: …»), echoing the field names of the composer instruction, and the lowercase veto rejected all three. Both language instructions now ask for two or three plain sentences of prose starting with a capital letter, with no labels, no key: value lines and no list, naming the file of seen.document, its page count, each heading inside quotation marks and the opening of the text exactly as read; the projected opening is cut to 450 characters at a sentence end, never at the dot of a numbered heading. Offline composer probe over the real receipt: faithful English and Spanish finals.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


